  "summary": "ACCEPT. The corrected plan is feasible, internally consistent, architecture-aligned, failure-complete, and testable against the current production seams. PRC3-001 is closed normatively: one single-flight pair coordinator must fill durable capacity by launching independently scoped runners without awaiting prior Workers; completion is only a wake-up; limits two and four require observable simultaneous execution; 4-to-1 preserves leases and suppresses replacements; 1-to-4 fills newly available slots; durable closure stops launches; reconciliation requires local drain plus fresh durable terminal exhaustion; and a sequential coordinator is explicitly nonconforming and fails the barrier tests. QR-001 through QR-005 also remain closed: authenticated Start is composed through claim, packet, Worker, commit/failure, probe, drain, reconciliation, and terminal status; provider recovery uses exactly five fixed source-free active probes with no sixth, startup sweep, or background resume; navigation is double-bound to the current job version and unexpired lease before evidence release and receipt mutation; completed replay reconstructs the full persisted canonical Document graph including cardinalities; and production-composed authenticated PostgreSQL plus Windows-host qualification proves the reachable runtime. Story 12.1 and Story 12.2 contracts, immutable Documents, the approved host topology, bounded navigate_code, and Story 12.4/12.5/CodeGraphContext exclusions are preserved. The hash-bound plan is ready for the repository-mandated planned-change authorization before task regeneration."
